{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-49902" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{3}^{4}\\frac{4x}{(x-2)^{2}}\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-49902" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4x}{(x-2)^{2}} & =\\frac{A}{(x-2)}+\\frac{B}{(x-2)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,$ and $B,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x-2)^{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n4x=A(x-2)+B.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=2,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(2) & =A(2-2)+B \\\\ 8 & =0+B \\\\ B & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known value of $B,$ we can solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(0) & =A(0-2)+B \\\\ 0 & =-2A+B \\\\ 0 & =-2A+8 \\\\ A & =\\frac{8}{2} \\\\ A & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum\n\n$$\n\\frac{4x}{(x-2)^{2}}=\\frac{4}{(x-2)}+\\frac{8}{(x-2)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{4}\\frac{4x}{(x-2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}(\\frac{4}{(x-2)}+\\frac{8}{(x-2)^{2}})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{3}^{4}\\frac{1}{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x+8{\\int }_{3}^{4}\\frac{1}{(x-2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|{|}_{3}^{4}+8(-\\frac{1}{x-2}){|}_{3}^{4} \\\\  & =4(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4-2|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3-2|)+8(-\\frac{1}{4-2}+\\frac{1}{3-2}) \\\\  & =4(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4-2|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3-2|)+8(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-49902" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c238dc013e93696dca3a4c4c9ddb4498ed87910f0e9671a8aac9473b41e03cf"} {"question" "q-49902" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-49902" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+6"] ["math" "-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-2"] ["math" "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+4"] ["math" "5\\operatorname{ln}⁡5+4"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-49902" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-348426" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x+1}{(x+5)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-348426" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+1}{(x+5)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x+5}+\\frac{B}{(x+5)^{2}}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,$ and $B,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x+5)^{2}$ and get\n\n$$\nx+1=A(x+5)+B.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-5,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5+1 & =A(-5+5)+B \\\\ B & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known value of $B,$ we can solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0+1 & =A(0+5)-4 \\\\ 1 & =5A-4 \\\\ 5A & =5 \\\\ A & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+1}{(x+5)^{2}}=\\frac{1}{x+5}-\\frac{4}{(x+5)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x+1}{(x+5)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{1}{x+5}-\\frac{4}{(x+5)^{2}})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{x+5}\\,\\text{d}x-4{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{(x+5)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+5|\\,{|}_{0}^{1}+\\frac{4}{x+5}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+5|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|0+5|)+(\\frac{4}{1+5}-\\frac{4}{0+5}) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡6-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5)+(\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{4}{5}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{6}{5})-\\frac{2}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-348426" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c238dc013e93696dca3a4c4c9ddb4498ed87910f0e9671a8aac9473b41e03cf"} {"question" "q-348426" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-348426" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\ln(6)-\\ln(5)-\\frac{2}{15}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-346710" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{x+2}{(x-4)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-346710" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+2}{(x-4)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x-4}+\\frac{B}{(x-4)^{2}}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,$ and $B,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x-4)^{2}$ and get\n\n$$\nx+2=A(x-4)+B.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=4,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4+2 & =A(4-4)+B \\\\ B & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known value of $B,$ we can solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0+2 & =A(0-4)+6 \\\\ 2 & =-4A+6 \\\\ 4A & =4 \\\\ A & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+2}{(x-4)^{2}}=\\frac{1}{x-4}+\\frac{6}{(x-4)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{x+2}{(x-4)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(\\frac{1}{x-4}+\\frac{6}{(x-4)^{2}})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x+6{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{(x-4)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|\\,{|}_{1}^{2}-\\frac{6}{x-4}\\,{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2-4|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1-4|)-(\\frac{6}{2-4}-\\frac{6}{1-4}) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)-(-3-(-2)) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{2}{3})+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-346710" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c238dc013e93696dca3a4c4c9ddb4498ed87910f0e9671a8aac9473b41e03cf"} {"question" "q-346710" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-346710" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1+\\ln(2)-\\ln(3)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-115323" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{4x-10}{(x-2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-115323" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4x-10}{(x-2)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{(x-2)}+\\frac{B}{(x-2)^{2}}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,$ and $B,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x-2)^{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n4x-10=A(x-2)+B.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=2,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(2)-10 & =A(2-2)+B \\\\ -2 & =0+B \\\\ B & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known value of $B,$ we can solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(0)-10 & =A(0-2)+B \\\\ -10 & =-2A-2 \\\\ -2A & =-8 \\\\ A & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum\n\n$$\n\\frac{4x-10}{(x-2)^{2}}=\\frac{4}{(x-2)}-\\frac{2}{(x-2)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4x-10}{(x-2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{4}{(x-2)}-\\frac{2}{(x-2)^{2}})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int \\frac{1}{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int \\frac{1}{(x-2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|-2(-\\frac{1}{x-2})+C \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+\\frac{2}{x-2}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-115323" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c238dc013e93696dca3a4c4c9ddb4498ed87910f0e9671a8aac9473b41e03cf"} {"question" "q-115323" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-115323" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|-\\frac{4}{x-2}+C"] ["math" "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+\\frac{2}{x-2}+C"] ["math" "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|-\\frac{2}{(x-2)^{2}}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+\\frac{4}{x-2}+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+\\frac{1}{(x-2)^{2}}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-115323" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+\\frac{2}{x-2}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-348350" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x+3}{(x-5)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-348350" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+3}{(x-5)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x-5}+\\frac{B}{(x-5)^{2}}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,$ and $B,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x-5)^{2}$ and get\n\n$$\nx+3=A(x-5)+B.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=5,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5+3 & =A(5-5)+B \\\\ B & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known value of $B,$ we can solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0+3 & =A(0-5)+8 \\\\ 3 & =-5A+8 \\\\ 5A & =5 \\\\ A & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+3}{(x-5)^{2}}=\\frac{1}{x-5}+\\frac{8}{(x-5)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x+3}{(x-5)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{1}{x-5}+\\frac{8}{(x-5)^{2}})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{x-5}\\,\\text{d}x+8{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{(x-5)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-5|\\,{|}_{0}^{1}-\\frac{8}{x-5}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1-5|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|0-5|)-(\\frac{8}{1-5}-\\frac{8}{0-5}) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5)-(-2-(-\\frac{8}{5})) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{5})+\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-348350" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c238dc013e93696dca3a4c4c9ddb4498ed87910f0e9671a8aac9473b41e03cf"} {"question" "q-348350" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-348350" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\ln(4)-\\ln(5)+\\frac{2}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-11340" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{5x+35}{(x+2)^{2}(x-3)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-11340" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5x+35}{(x+2)^{2}(x-3)}=\\frac{A}{(x+2)}+\\frac{B}{(x+2)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{(x-3)}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,$ $B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x+2)^{2}(x-3)$ and get\n\n$$\n5x+35=A(x+2)(x-3)+B(x-3)+C(x+2)^{2}.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-2,$ we can eliminate $A$ and $C$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(-2)+35 & =A(-2+2)(-2-3)+B(-2-3)+C(-2+2)^{2} \\\\ -10+35 & =B(-5) \\\\ B & =\\frac{25}{-5} \\\\ B & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=3,$ we can eliminate $A$ and $B$ and solve for $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(3)+35 & =A(3+2)(3-3)+B(3-3)+C(3+2)^{2} \\\\ 15+35 & =C{(5)}^{2} \\\\ C & =\\frac{50}{25} \\\\ C & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known values of $B$ and $C,$ we can solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(0)+35 & =A(0+2)(0-3)+B(0-3)+C(0+2)^{2} \\\\ 35 & =-6A-3B+4C \\\\ 35 & =-6A-3(-5)+4(2) \\\\ 35 & =-6A+23 \\\\ 6A & =-35+23 \\\\ A & =\\frac{-12}{6} \\\\ A & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{5x+35}{(x+2)^{2}(x-3)}=-\\frac{2}{(x+2)}-\\frac{5}{(x+2)^{2}}+\\frac{2}{(x-3)}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5x+35}{(x+2)^{2}(x-3)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-\\frac{2}{(x+2)}-\\frac{5}{(x+2)^{2}}+\\frac{2}{(x-3)})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\int \\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x-5\\int \\frac{1}{(x+2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+\\frac{5}{x+2}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+K,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K$ is an integral constant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-11340" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c238dc013e93696dca3a4c4c9ddb4498ed87910f0e9671a8aac9473b41e03cf"} {"question" "q-11340" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-11340" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+\\frac{5}{x+2}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+K"] ["math" "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+\\frac{3}{x-3}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+K"] ["math" "-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+\\frac{2}{x+2}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+K"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|-\\frac{2}{x-3}+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+K"] ["math" "5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+\\frac{2}{x-3}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+K"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-11340" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+\\frac{5}{x+2}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+K"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-11373" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{14{x}^{2}+47x+42}{(2x+3)^{2}(x+3)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-11373" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{14{x}^{2}+47x+42}{(2x+3)^{2}(x+3)}=\\frac{A}{(2x+3)}+\\frac{B}{(2x+3)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{(x+3)}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,$ $B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(2x+3)^{2}(x+3)$ and get\n\n$$\n14{x}^{2}+47x+42=A(2x+3)(x+3)+B(x+3)+C(2x+3)^{2}.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-\\frac{3}{2},$ we can eliminate $A$ and $C$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14{(-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}+47(-\\frac{3}{2})+42 & =A(2(-\\frac{3}{2})+3)(-\\frac{3}{2}+3) \\\\  & +B(-\\frac{3}{2}+3)+C{(2(-\\frac{3}{2})+3)}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{63}{2}-\\frac{141}{2}+42 & =B(\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{63-141+84}{2} & =B(\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\ B & =-\\frac{12}{6} \\\\ B & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-3,$ we can eliminate $A$ and $B$ and solve for $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14(-3)^{2}+47(-3)+42 & =A(2(-3)+3)(-3+3)+B(-3+3)+C(2(-3)+3)^{2} \\\\ 126-141+42 & =C{(-3)}^{2} \\\\ C & =\\frac{27}{9} \\\\ C & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known values of $B$ and $C,$ we can solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14({0}^{2})+47(0)+42 & =A(2(0)+3)(0+3)+B(0+3)+C(2(0)+3)^{2} \\\\ 42 & =9A+3B+9C \\\\ 42 & =9A+3(2)+9(3) \\\\ 42 & =9A+33 \\\\ 9A & =42-33 \\\\ A & =\\frac{9}{9} \\\\ A & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{14{x}^{2}+47x+42}{(2x+3)^{2}(x+3)}=\\frac{1}{(2x+3)}+\\frac{2}{(2x+3)^{2}}+\\frac{3}{(x+3)}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{14{x}^{2}+47x+42}{(2x+3)^{2}(x+3)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{(2x+3)}+\\frac{2}{(2x+3)^{2}}+\\frac{3}{(x+3)})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{(2x+3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+3\\int \\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+3|-\\frac{1}{2x+3}+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+K,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K$ is an integral constant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-11373" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c238dc013e93696dca3a4c4c9ddb4498ed87910f0e9671a8aac9473b41e03cf"} {"question" "q-11373" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-11373" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+3|+\\frac{2}{2x+3}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+K"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+3|-\\frac{1}{2x+3}+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+K"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+3|+\\frac{1}{2x+3}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+K"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+3|+\\frac{3}{2x+3}-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+K"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+3|-\\frac{3}{2x+3}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+K"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-11373" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+3|-\\frac{1}{2x+3}+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+K"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-49785" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{5{x}^{2}+6}{{x}^{2}(2x+3)}=-\\frac{4}{3x}+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{23}{3(2x+3)},\n$$\n\ncalculate $\\int \\frac{5{x}^{2}+6}{(2x+3){x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-49785" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We rewrite our integral and integrate term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5{x}^{2}+6}{{x}^{2}(2x+3)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-\\frac{4}{3x}+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{23}{3(2x+3)})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{23}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{23}{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+3|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-49785" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c238dc013e93696dca3a4c4c9ddb4498ed87910f0e9671a8aac9473b41e03cf"} {"question" "q-49785" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-49785" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{23}{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+3|+C"] ["math" "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\frac{5}{3x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+3|+C"] ["math" "\\frac{23}{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\frac{1}{x}-\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+3|+C"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\frac{1}{2x}+\\frac{6}{23}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+3|+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\frac{23}{6}\\frac{1}{x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+3|+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-49785" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{23}{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+3|+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-348473" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{8-x}{x(x-4)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-348473" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{8-x}{x(x-4)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{x-4}+\\frac{C}{(x-4)^{2}}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,$ $B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $x(x-4)^{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n8-x=A(x-4)^{2}+Bx(x-4)+Cx.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0,$ we can eliminate $B$ and $C$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8-0 & =A(0-4)^{2}+B(0)(0-4)+C(0) \\\\ 8 & =16A \\\\ A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=4,$ we can eliminate $A$ and $B$ and solve for $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8-4 & =A(4-4)^{2}+B(4)(4-4)+C(4) \\\\ 4 & =4C \\\\ C & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=1$ and substituting the known values of $A$ and $C,$ we can solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8-1 & =A(1-4)^{2}+B(1)(1-4)+C(1) \\\\ 7 & =9A-3B+C \\\\ 7 & =9(\\frac{1}{2})-3B+1 \\\\ B & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{8-x}{x(x-4)^{2}}=\\frac{1}{2x}-\\frac{1}{2(x-4)}+\\frac{1}{(x-4)^{2}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{8-x}{x(x-4)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(\\frac{1}{2x}-\\frac{1}{2(x-4)}+\\frac{1}{(x-4)^{2}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x-\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{(x-4)^{2}}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|\\,{|}_{1}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|\\,{|}_{1}^{2}-\\frac{1}{x-4}\\,{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)-(-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}+\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-348473" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c238dc013e93696dca3a4c4c9ddb4498ed87910f0e9671a8aac9473b41e03cf"} {"question" "q-348473" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-348473" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}\\ln(3)+\\frac{1}{6}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-11369" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{-9x+27}{(1-x)^{2}(x+5)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-11369" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{-9x+27}{(1-x)^{2}(x+5)}=\\frac{A}{(1-x)}+\\frac{B}{(1-x)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{(x+5)}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,$ $B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(1-x)^{2}(x+5)$ and get\n\n$$\n-9x+27=A(1-x)(x+5)+B(x+5)+C(1-x)^{2}.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=1,$ we can eliminate $A$ and $C$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9(1)+27 & =A(1-1)(1+5)+B(1+5)+C(1-1)^{2} \\\\ -9+27 & =B(6) \\\\ B & =\\frac{18}{6} \\\\ B & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-5,$ we can eliminate $A$ and $B$ and solve for $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9(-5)+27 & =A(1-(-5))(-5+5)+B(-5+5)+C(1-(-5))^{2} \\\\ -45+27 & =C{(6)}^{2} \\\\ C & =\\frac{72}{36} \\\\ C & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known values of $B$ and $C,$ we can solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9(0)+27 & =A(1-0)(0+5)+B(0+5)+C(1-0)^{2} \\\\ 27 & =5A+5B+C \\\\ 27 & =5A+5(3)+2 \\\\ 27 & =5A+17 \\\\ 5A & =27-17 \\\\ A & =\\frac{10}{5} \\\\ A & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{-9x+27}{(1-x)^{2}(x+5)}=\\frac{2}{(1-x)}+\\frac{3}{(1-x)^{2}}+\\frac{2}{(x+5)}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{-9x+27}{(1-x)^{2}(x+5)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2}{(1-x)}+\\frac{3}{(1-x)^{2}}+\\frac{2}{(x+5)})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{1-x}\\,\\text{d}x+3\\int \\frac{1}{(1-x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{x+5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1-x|+\\frac{3}{1-x}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+5|+K,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K$ is an integral constant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-11369" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c238dc013e93696dca3a4c4c9ddb4498ed87910f0e9671a8aac9473b41e03cf"} {"question" "q-11369" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-11369" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1-x|+\\frac{3}{1-x}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+5|+K"] ["math" "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1-x|-\\frac{2}{1-x}+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+5|+K"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1-x|+\\frac{3}{1-x}-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+5|+K"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1-x|-\\frac{3}{1-x}+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+5|+K"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1-x|-\\frac{2}{1-x}+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+5|+K"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-11369" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1-x|+\\frac{3}{1-x}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+5|+K"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-348521" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{2}^{5}\\frac{2-x}{{x}^{2}-12x+36}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-348521" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's first factor the denominator of the integrand:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2-x}{{x}^{2}-12x+36}=\\frac{2-x}{(x-6)^{2}}\n$$\n\nWe must convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2-x}{(x-6)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x-6}+\\frac{B}{(x-6)^{2}}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A$ and $B,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x-6)^{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n2-x=A(x-6)+B.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=6,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-6 & =A(6-6)+B \\\\ B & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known value of $B,$ we can solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-0 & =A(0-6)-4 \\\\ 2 & =-6A-4 \\\\ A & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2-x}{(x-6)^{2}}=-\\frac{1}{x-6}-\\frac{4}{(x-6)^{2}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\frac{2-x}{(x-6)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}(-\\frac{1}{x-6}-\\frac{4}{(x-6)^{2}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\frac{1}{x-6}\\,\\text{d}x-4{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\frac{1}{(x-6)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-6|\\,{|}_{2}^{5}+4\\cdot \\frac{1}{x-6}\\,{|}_{2}^{5} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)+4(-1-(-\\frac{1}{4})) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡4+4(-\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-348521" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c238dc013e93696dca3a4c4c9ddb4498ed87910f0e9671a8aac9473b41e03cf"} {"question" "q-348521" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-348521" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\ln(4)-3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-348617" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-6}^{-5}\\frac{3x+7}{{x}^{2}+8x+16}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-348617" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's first factor the denominator of the integrand:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3x+7}{{x}^{2}+8x+16}=\\frac{3x+7}{(x+4)^{2}}\n$$\n\nWe must convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3x+7}{(x+4)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x+4}+\\frac{B}{(x+4)^{2}}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A$ and $B,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x+4)^{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n3x+7=A(x+4)+B.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-4,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(-4)+7 & =A(-4+4)+B \\\\ B & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known value of $B,$ we can solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(0)+7 & =A(0+4)-5 \\\\ 7 & =4A-5 \\\\ A & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3x+7}{(x+4)^{2}}=\\frac{3}{x+4}-\\frac{5}{(x+4)^{2}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-6}^{-5}\\frac{3x+7}{(x+4)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-6}^{-5}(\\frac{3}{x+4}-\\frac{5}{(x+4)^{2}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{-6}^{-5}\\frac{1}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x-5{\\int }_{-6}^{-5}\\frac{1}{(x+4)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+4|\\,{|}_{-6}^{-5}+5\\cdot \\frac{1}{x+4}\\,{|}_{-6}^{-5} \\\\  & =3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)+5(-1-(-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})+5(-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-348617" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c238dc013e93696dca3a4c4c9ddb4498ed87910f0e9671a8aac9473b41e03cf"} {"question" "q-348617" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-348617" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3\\ln(2)-\\frac{5}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-115537" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{4{x}^{2}-12x+4}{{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+4x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-115537" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's first factor the denominator of the integrand:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4{x}^{2}-12x+4}{{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+4x}=\\frac{4{x}^{2}-12x+4}{x(x-2)^{2}}\n$$\n\nWe must convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4{x}^{2}-12x+4}{x(x-2)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{x-2}+\\frac{C}{(x-2)^{2}}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $x(x-2)^{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}-12x+4=A(x-2)^{2}+Bx(x-2)+Cx.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=2,$ we can eliminate $A$ and $B$ and solve for $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(2)^{2}-12(2)+4 & =A(2-2)^{2}+B(2)(2-2)+C(2) \\\\ -4 & =2C \\\\ C & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, plugging in $x=0,$ we can eliminate $B$ and $C$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(0)^{2}-12(0)+4 & =A(0-2)^{2}+B(0)(0-2)+C(0) \\\\ 4 & =4A \\\\ A & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=1$ and substituting the known values of $A$ and $C,$ we can solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(1)^{2}-12(1)+4 & =A(1-2)^{2}+B(1)(1-2)+C(1) \\\\ -4 & =A-B+C \\\\ -4 & =1-B+(-2) \\\\ -3 & =-B \\\\ B & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum\n\n$$\n\\frac{4{x}^{2}-12x+4}{{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+4x}=\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{3}{x-2}-\\frac{2}{(x-2)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4{x}^{2}-12x+4}{{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{3}{x-2}-\\frac{2}{(x-2)^{2}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+3\\int \\frac{1}{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int \\frac{1}{(x-2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+\\frac{2}{x-2}+K,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K$ is an integral constant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-115537" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/refere