r the denominator of the integrand:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{5{t}^{2}+20t+6}{{t}^{3}+2{t}^{2}+t}\\,\\text{d}t=\\int \\frac{5{t}^{2}+20t+6}{t(t+1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe must convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5{t}^{2}+20t+6}{t(t+1)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{t}+\\frac{B}{t+1}+\\frac{C}{(t+1)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $t(t+1)^{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n5{t}^{2}+20t+6=A(t+1)^{2}+B(t)(t+1)+C(t).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $t=0,$ we can eliminate $B$ and $C$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(0)^{2}+20(0)+6 & =A(0+1)^{2}+B(0)(0+1)+C(0) \\\\ 6 & =A \\\\ A & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, plugging in $t=-1,$ we can eliminate $A$ and $B$ and solve for $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(-1)^{2}+20(-1)+6 & =A(-1+1)^{2}+B(-1)(-1+1)+C(-1) \\\\ -9 & =-C \\\\ C & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $t=1$ and substituting the known values of $A$ and $C,$ we can solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(1)^{2}+20(1)+6 & =A(1+1)^{2}+B(1)(1+1)+C(1) \\\\ 31 & =4A+2B+C \\\\ 31 & =4(6)+2B+(9) \\\\ B & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum\n\n$$\n\\frac{5{t}^{2}+20t+6}{t(t+1)^{2}}=\\frac{6}{t}-\\frac{1}{t+1}+\\frac{9}{(t+1)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5{t}^{2}+20t+6}{t(t+1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int (\\frac{(6)}{t}+\\frac{(-1)}{t+1}+\\frac{(9)}{(t+1)^{2}})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =6\\int \\frac{1}{t}\\,\\text{d}t-\\int \\frac{1}{t+1}\\,\\text{d}t+9\\int \\frac{1}{(t+1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t+1|-\\frac{9}{t+1}+K,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K$ is an integral constant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-3612" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c238dc013e93696dca3a4c4c9ddb4498ed87910f0e9671a8aac9473b41e03cf"} {"question" "q-3612" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-3612" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "6\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t+1|-\\frac{1}{t+1}+K"] ["math" "6\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t+1|-\\frac{2}{t+1}+K"] ["math" "6\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t+1|+\\frac{9}{t+1}+K"] ["math" "6\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t+1|-\\frac{9}{t+1}+K"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t+1|+\\frac{9}{t+1}+K"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-3612" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t+1|-\\frac{9}{t+1}+K"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-346752" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{x-4}{{x}^{2}-2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-346752" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's first factor the denominator of the integrand:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-4}{{x}^{2}-2x+1}=\\frac{x-4}{(x-1)^{2}}\n$$\n\nWe must convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-4}{(x-1)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x-1}+\\frac{B}{(x-1)^{2}}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A$ and $B,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x-1)^{2}$ and get\n\n$$\nx-4=A(x-1)+B.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=1,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-4 & =A(1-1)+B \\\\ B & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known value of $B,$ we can solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0-4 & =A(0-1)+B \\\\ -4 & =-A-3 \\\\ A & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-4}{(x-1)^{2}}=\\frac{1}{x-1}-\\frac{3}{(x-1)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{x-4}{(x-1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}(\\frac{1}{x-1}-\\frac{3}{(x-1)^{2}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x-3{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{(x-1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|\\,{|}_{2}^{4}+3\\cdot \\frac{1}{x-1}\\,{|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)+3(\\frac{1}{3}-1) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{1})+3(-\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-346752" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c238dc013e93696dca3a4c4c9ddb4498ed87910f0e9671a8aac9473b41e03cf"} {"question" "q-346752" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-346752" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\ln(3)-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-115623" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{4{x}^{2}}{(2x+1)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-115623" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we must convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{(2x+1)^{3}}=\\frac{A}{2x+1}+\\frac{B}{(2x+1)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{(2x+1)^{3}}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(2x+1)^{3}$ and get\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}=A(2x+1)^{2}+B(2x+1)+C.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-\\frac{1}{2},$ we can eliminate $A$ and $B$ and solve for $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & =A{(2\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})+1)}^{2}+B(2\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})+1)+C \\\\ 1 & =C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known value of $C,$ we get an equation relating $A$ and $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(0)^{2} & =A(2(0)+1)^{2}+B(2(0)+1)+C \\\\ 0 & =A+B+1 \\\\ A+B & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, plugging in $x=-1$ and substituting the known value of $C,$ we get an equation relating $A$ and $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(-1)^{2} & =A(2(-1)+1)^{2}+B(2(-1)+1)+C \\\\ 4 & =A-B+1 \\\\ A-B & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the equations $A-B=3$ and $A+B=-1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2A & =3-1 \\\\ A & =1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand substituting back into $A+B=-1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+B & =-1 \\\\ B & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{(2x+1)^{3}}=\\frac{1}{2x+1}-\\frac{2}{(2x+1)^{2}}+\\frac{1}{(2x+1)^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4{x}^{2}}{(2x+1)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{2x+1}-\\frac{2}{(2x+1)^{2}}+\\frac{1}{(2x+1)^{3}})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int \\frac{1}{(2x+1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{(2x+1)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|+\\frac{1}{2x+1}-\\frac{1}{4(2x+1)^{2}}+K,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K$ is an integral constant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-115623" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c238dc013e93696dca3a4c4c9ddb4498ed87910f0e9671a8aac9473b41e03cf"} {"question" "q-115623" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-115623" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|+\\frac{1}{2x+1}-\\frac{1}{4(2x+1)^{2}}+K"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|-\\frac{1}{4(2x+1)^{2}}+K"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|+\\frac{2}{2x+1}+\\frac{1}{2(2x+1)^{2}}+K"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|+\\frac{1}{2x+1}-\\frac{3}{4(2x+1)^{2}}+K"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|-\\frac{1}{2x+1}+\\frac{1}{(2x+1)^{2}}+K"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-115623" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|+\\frac{1}{2x+1}-\\frac{1}{4(2x+1)^{2}}+K"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-115662" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{x-2}{(x+8)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-115662" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we must convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-2}{(x+8)^{3}}=\\frac{A}{x+8}+\\frac{B}{(x+8)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{(x+8)^{3}}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x+8)^{3}$ and get\n\n$$\nx-2=A(x+8)^{2}+B(x+8)+C.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-8,$ we can eliminate $A$ and $B$ and solve for $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-8)-2 & =A(-8+8)^{2}+B(-8+8)+C \\\\ -10 & =C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=-7$ and substituting the known value of $C,$ we get an equation relating $A$ and $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-7)-2 & =A(-7+8)^{2}+B(-7+8)+C \\\\ -9 & =A+B-10 \\\\ A+B & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, plugging in $x=-9$ and substituting the known value of $C,$ we get an equation relating $A$ and $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-9)-2 & =A(-9+8)^{2}+B(-9+8)+C \\\\ -11 & =A-B-10 \\\\ A-B & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the equations $A-B=-1$ and $A+B=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2A & =-1+1 \\\\ 2A & =0 \\\\ A & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand substituting back into $A+B=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0+B & =1 \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-2}{(x+8)^{3}}=\\frac{1}{(x+8)^{2}}-\\frac{10}{(x+8)^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x-2}{(x+8)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{(x+8)^{2}}-\\frac{10}{(x+8)^{3}})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{(x+8)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x-10\\int \\frac{1}{(x+8)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{x+8}+\\frac{5}{(x+8)^{2}}+K,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K$ is an integral constant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cda99641b1"} {"question" "q-115662" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c238dc013e93696dca3a4c4c9ddb4498ed87910f0e9671a8aac9473b41e03cf"} {"question" "q-115662" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad4dbd3ec8405462ccdab0221832d812651cfd8e53c0fd49077d50cd